{"authored" [{"question" "q-127043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector parallel to the line that points in the direction of increasing $t$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/review.json" "file_sha256" "77158f3b69d2fbadbf03b2bbf325083404203d896965fc983923878d24ea8cb9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cf9b0fc82e73060e35594f297203fff220e09551533aa770b1f090888ce275ab" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/verification.json" "basis" 1539 "rationale" "The original request asks for a parallel vector and displays both v and -v, so two choices are mathematically correct. The site actually graded the coefficient vector v (option e) Correct. The authorized study correction adds orientation in the direction of increasing t, making e the unique valid displayed choice. All original DOM, screenshots, solver decisions, grades, choices, field and answer identities remain retained."} {"question" "q-127043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Write the position vector as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\5\\\\\\frac17\\end{pmatrix}\n+t\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac13\\\\-4\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFor any positive increment $h$,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t+h)-\\mathbf r(t)=h\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac13\\\\-4\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\left(\\frac13,-4,2\\right)$ is parallel to the line and points in the direction of increasing $t$. Its negative $\\left(-\\frac13,4,-2\\right)$ is also parallel, but points in the direction of decreasing $t$ and does not satisfy the requested orientation." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/review.json" "file_sha256" "77158f3b69d2fbadbf03b2bbf325083404203d896965fc983923878d24ea8cb9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cf9b0fc82e73060e35594f297203fff220e09551533aa770b1f090888ce275ab" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/verification.json" "basis" 1539 "rationale" "The original request asks for a parallel vector and displays both v and -v, so two choices are mathematically correct. The site actually graded the coefficient vector v (option e) Correct. The authorized study correction adds orientation in the direction of increasing t, making e the unique valid displayed choice. All original DOM, screenshots, solver decisions, grades, choices, field and answer identities remain retained."} {"question" "q-127043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/review.json" "file_sha256" "77158f3b69d2fbadbf03b2bbf325083404203d896965fc983923878d24ea8cb9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "cf9b0fc82e73060e35594f297203fff220e09551533aa770b1f090888ce275ab" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-127043/verification.json" "basis" 1539 "rationale" "The original request asks for a parallel vector and displays both v and -v, so two choices are mathematically correct. The site actually graded the coefficient vector v (option e) Correct. The authorized study correction adds orientation in the direction of increasing t, making e the unique valid displayed choice. All original DOM, screenshots, solver decisions, grades, choices, field and answer identities remain retained."} {"question" "q-127043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/state.json" "file_sha256" "7a1b921e5d245cef0108dc3ea1ba50291692ce37e6d5aaf037ec25a0bef35e3f" "basis" 1538 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ 5-4t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t \\\\ -4t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,5,\\frac{1}{7})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/ma